# Canonical source path fix: independent review

Scope: commit 152c7d485aeb7339b0bc8448bef09bca40837a03 production host delta, compared with the immutable initial evidence ../review-canonical-code/manifest.json (SHA256 e667bf78d2393260ba5bec4de1effdc1f8e395f0ca4ca37ee02d9d5c77be76c5). No production edits. No migration/human approval inferred.

Fixed dependencies: base 0d80fe6289346a1b8481b03b149d5b35af90d68d plus original overlay-manifest.json and this snapshot.json. Workspace was a separate copy of the initial review workspace; six fixed files overlaid, independent probes under tools/src/bin only. Separate target directory. commit-match.json confirms six copied files and 441 present production/schema/design/test dependency files equal 152c7d4; remaining live documentation changes are outside this code review. workspace-files.json records exact scratch inputs. The old evidence, source copies, binaries and target were not overwritten.

Results: original unmodified 15-observation probe now rejects both reported failures. doc/real./input.nepld is rejected lexically rather than accepting the same Windows physical file as doc/real/input.nepld. doc/hash#name.nepld is rejected by both check and html before generation. Normal physical source check and HTML still pass. A real Windows repository-internal junction remains rejected by bounded access. Stale MD/source/alias bytes, unknown alias target, malformed source, duplicate JSON, unknown fields and existing output rejection remain exercised.

Independent matrix: 27 component examples in each of source/projection/aliases/route, four casefold duplicate cases, and two real-parser LF/internal-body comparisons: 114 passed. It rejects empty/dot/parent/trailing-dot/trailing-space components, ASCII Windows device names with case/extension, punctuation #/%/colon/backslash/query/control, and Unicode. It accepts ordinary dot-containing names, hidden names, uppercase nonreserved names, COM0/COM10/CONSOLE. The stricter repository-host domain is intentional and documented in spec16; it does not alter Doc text or foundation Source URI. The manifest argument itself remains a caller-selected bounded repository path, distinct from registered entries. No new blocker found in this delta.

Final-LF delta: host generate trims only terminal LF delimiters from the already rendered Markdown and appends exactly one LF. The independent comparison to host::from_source checks every preceding body byte, including inter-paragraph separators. Actual chapter13 MD differs from before by precisely removal of one final LF (26271 -> 26270 bytes), not content rewriting. Canonical managed tests 4 passed; annotated_host managed test 1 passed. Unix-only symlink test was not run on this Windows host.

Actual fixed production CLI: doc-canonical --check and doc-canonical html each exit 0 under original default budgets. All three generated files are byte-identical to the initial positive: HTML 91421 bytes SHA256 99b80b99318619335eca6bebbcc2d0ec044f12c2c4fe35d5020dc53af4a355a1, CSS and manifest also exact. Manifest artifact hashes were checked. This is host-generation evidence, not new browser/GitHub anchor/human semantic approval or universal path portability certification. WASI/Linux/Unix were not rerun for this std filesystem adapter delta; no result is inferred for them. Deliberate concurrent filesystem mutation/TOCTOU is outside this bounded test.

Reproduction: commands.json, native-command.json and chapter-commands.json retain commands/cwd/status; source snapshots and probe.rs/matrix.rs retain exact code; binaries.json retains executable hashes and versions. To rebuild, reconstruct base plus original overlay then these six overlays, place probe.rs at tools/src/bin/review-canonical.rs and matrix.rs at tools/src/bin/review-path-matrix.rs, use a fresh target and fresh fixture/output paths. Windows junction setup: create fixture/doc/real then New-Item -ItemType Junction fixture/doc/linked -Target <absolute fixture/doc/real>. The original probe writes its own real inputs. Source hashes are in snapshots; expected invalid/valid values are explicit in matrix.rs. A first inline Python command list had a syntax typo and did not execute Cargo; corrected command execution is logged. No failed production run was hidden.
